s strong enough to dissolve  anything  if you remember harry potter's first  year at hogwarts there was a french  alchemist who actually discovered a way  to live forever nicola flamel although  there wasn't much need for alchemy but  the rise of the modern ministry of magic  an individual wizard could try to strike  gold by choosing this career  apparition examiner apparition wasn't  easy of all the magical skills that  young wizards and witches could be  trained in this ability to teleport from  one location to another was among the  most advanced and it was extremely  dangerous too  it wasn't uncommon for wizards and  witches to be tested on their ability by  an apparition examiner especially in the  united states as their job name implies  an apparition examiner judged an  individual's ability to safely use the  technique without causing harm to  themselves or others  bartender there were plenty of unique  magical jobs in the world of harry  potter but there were plenty of ordinary  ones as well if you grew up with a  magical ability you wouldn't be limited  to a career the ministry of magic or the  magical congress of the united states of  america  you could take an ordinary job as well  one of the most interesting professions  was a simple bartender whether at the  three broomsticks in the hogs head in or  any other pub a bartender had the task  of filling drink orders and running the  business behind a bar with innumerable  magical cocktails and drinks the job was  actually one of the more interesting  ones in the wizarding world  magical creatures breeder breeding  magical creatures was a particularly  sought after skill while some muggles  like dudley's aunt margery enjoyed  breeding bulldogs wizards and witches  could breed far more exotic creatures  although the career drew the attention  of the ministry of magic from time to  time who was concerned with the  mistreatment and abuse of magical  creatures breeders were by and large  free to spend their days with the  animals they loved lord stoddard withers  was one of the most famous wizard  breeders of his day he bred winged  horses and even used them to create a  new sport flying polo  others bred more domestic creatures the  nasal a cat-like animal with a xxx  classification from the ministry was  often bred in order to safeguard its  owner's home and possessions arabella  fig was a reputable nasal breeder in  britain during harry potter's time at  hogwarts and earned enough money to live  a comfortable life  curse breaker  curse breaking was a tough business  that's for sure just like a bomb squad  defuses the bomb a curse breaker defused  curses  you might remember that ron weasley's  older brother bill worked as a curse  breaker after graduating from hogwarts  in 1989  and it might not seem like it but curse  breaking was actually one of the most  lucrative careers you could have in the  wizarding world  gringotts wizarding bank often hired  curse breakers to go on international  expeditions  in search of ancient treasure that they  could add to their vaults beneath diagon  alley when a treasure was discovered a  curse breaker was tasked with  investigating what type of horrible  illness or monster protected it  once while looking for treasure in egypt  bill even had to fight against a mummy  as part of his job  dragonologist dragons are among the most  fascinating magical creatures in the  wizarding world for that reason many  young matches zoologists are drawn to  the field of dragonology where they  studied the biology society and history  of the winged creatures  by harry potter's time most dragons had  been moved to magical reserves  due to the encroachment of muggles in  their natural habitat  while studying dragons in these smaller  territories wasn't as wondrous as  studying them in the raw wilderness  dragonologists didn't seem to mind so  much  compared to other more lucrative careers  a life spent as a dragonologist wouldn't  make you particularly rich  but those drawn to the job were never  chasing money anyway  they become dragonologists because of  their love for chinese fireballs  hybridian blacks and the rest of their  scaled cousins  healer compared to muggles wizards and  witches had far better healthcare the  contrast was starker in the ancient  world as well  before the rise of modern medicines  entire muggle towns and counties could  be wiped out by a particularly nasty  strain of the flu or a bacteria that  infested the local drinking water  while these types of ailments presented  the same problems to the wizarding world  magical cures ensured those illnesses  were far less fatal for wizards and  witches  and as the centuries passed and the  modern muggle world developed its own  advanced magical treatments the magical  healers remained superior  the process for becoming a magical  healer was just as rigorous as becoming  a medical doctor if you ever want to  hold one of these rare positions at st  muggles hospital for magical melodies  and injuries then you have to be at the  top of your class  and receive top marks on your newts when  you compare a healer's job to a muggle  doctor you'll find a few interesting  differences  since magical charms and curses were so  creative a healer's magic had to be as  well  when a patient rolled into the hospital  with a boneless limb or a cursed hand  healers had to use all of their know-how  to figure out what spells and potions to  employ  duelist in the second wizarding wars  it's hard to imagine dueling as anything  other than a way to win battles with  lord voldemort and his death eaters  standing against dumbledore in the  ministry of magic harry potter and his  peers study dueling  in order to prepare themselves for the  inevitable and tragic battles to come  but outside of warfare dueling had  another role in the wizarding world  just like quidditch dueling was a sport  and a natural outlet for young wizards  aggression and physical energy although  careers as a dualist were not very  lucrative with only the top combatants  earning a decent living many young  students often dreamed of becoming one  troll trainer when it comes to large  powerful creatures there are few  stronger than trolls and that makes them  the perfect security guards  although they're not very smart some  species of trolls could be trained and  assigned to protect wizards and witches  in the wizarding world  the process of training these trolls was  given to a troll trainer and it was a  fairly decent job for someone with a  knack for it  as you might expect training trolls  isn't without its fair share of hurdles  the gigantic creatures were clumsy at  best and deliberately murderous at worst  it wouldn't be uncommon for a trainer to  fly halfway across a room after  receiving a backhand from their troll  but the risk of bodily harm wasn't  enough to stop trainers from  participating in the profitable business  well there you have it 10 bizarre but  lucrative careers in the wizarding world  what do you think of them has it steered  you away from a potential life as an  aura at the ministry or as a professor  at hogwarts let me know which job you'd  choose in the comments below and if  you'd like to learn more about the  hundreds of other jobs unique to the  wizarding world be sure to leave that in  your comments as well  until next time remember  it does not do to dwell on dreams and  forget to live  [Music]

